Z||000005||Leper||09-22-2001||01:27 AM||||Formula88 the dogbone is the mount on the top of the engine. The driveline absorber looks like a shock absorber and is used as a front lower motor mount. You used to be able to get them at parts stores, but lateley, I havent been able to find one (on mine, the shock is good, but the rubber bushings in it are gone.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||09-22-2001||03:58 AM||||Rodney, the upper engine strut is the "dogbone" -- they are still available from GM here in the states I know - the OEM part number is #10046818 for the V-6 ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-22-2001||02:17 PM||||I forgot about those shock type ones... those have become nearly extict since most car makers seemed to have gaven up on using them.<P>Last I remember most of the aftermarket was replacing the shock type with a simple dogbone. I think PFKB (www.pontiacfiero.com) makes one of these. I don't know much about those people. They haven't updated their web site in I don't know how long.||||reg||1
